{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00284",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.73,
      "end_seconds": 7.37,
      "duration_seconds": 6.64,
      "text": "Hi doctor, sorry, the lift was out and I had to take the stairs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.89,
      "end_seconds": 13.3,
      "duration_seconds": 5.41,
      "text": "Of course, put it down anywhere. So, how can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.75,
      "end_seconds": 21.96,
      "duration_seconds": 7.21,
      "text": "It's exhaustion since I had the flu. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.96,
      "end_seconds": 27.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Right, how far back does it go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.51,
      "end_seconds": 35.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "Oh, it's been like this since last Tuesday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.38,
      "end_seconds": 40.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "On a a normal day, how strong is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.21,
      "end_seconds": 43.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "Severe, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.15,
      "end_seconds": 48.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "is there anything that triggers it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.09,
      "end_seconds": 53.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "I notice it more with walking far"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.86,
      "end_seconds": 56.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "Any aching legs as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.74,
      "end_seconds": 79.95,
      "duration_seconds": 22.21,
      "text": "I mean, yes, about the same, two months with aching legs, maybe a four out of ten on a bad day it's once or twice a day i've had brain fog too, for ten days about brain fog, I'd call it moderate"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.22,
      "end_seconds": 83.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Has there been any swollen legs?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.21,
      "end_seconds": 88.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "no, none, no swollen legs"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.99,
      "end_seconds": 95.4,
      "duration_seconds": 5.41,
      "text": "so, and what about chest pain, shortness of breath or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.16,
      "end_seconds": 100.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "No, none of that at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.02,
      "end_seconds": 105.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.2,
      "end_seconds": 108.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "nothing like that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.43,
      "end_seconds": 128.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "Tell me about your health in general, any ongoing conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.99,
      "end_seconds": 133.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "yeah, I have asthma, for two years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.89,
      "end_seconds": 138.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Which tablets or creams or inhalers do you use?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.01,
      "end_seconds": 143.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "Seretide inhaler. I take it twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.18,
      "end_seconds": 165.34,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "What about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.59,
      "end_seconds": 168.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "My father had kidney stones."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.31,
      "end_seconds": 183.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.97,
      "end_seconds": 200.23,
      "duration_seconds": 15.26,
      "text": "I have a couple of drinks on the weekend. It's just me and my wife at home now. I go to the gym a couple of times a week. I'm mostly vegetarian"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.98,
      "end_seconds": 206.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.18,
      "end_seconds": 208.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "no allergies"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.46,
      "end_seconds": 215.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Let me check your vitals now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.05,
      "end_seconds": 227.67,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Hold still for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.33,
      "end_seconds": 256.16,
      "duration_seconds": 6.83,
      "text": "Okay: SpO2 97 percent on room air, BP is 116 over 79, heart rate 77."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 257.83,
      "end_seconds": 259.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.97,
      "end_seconds": 263.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "I'll come back to those numbers."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.96,
      "end_seconds": 267.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Okay, a quick examination now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.76,
      "end_seconds": 270.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "let me just check something"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.86,
      "end_seconds": 289.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Chest sounds clear all over."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.61,
      "end_seconds": 303.85,
      "duration_seconds": 10.24,
      "text": "Right, you can sit back down. Let me tell you where I've got to. This is probably post-viral fatigue. I'd also keep anaemia in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 304.61,
      "end_seconds": 306.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "doctor, is this dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.75,
      "end_seconds": 342.35,
      "duration_seconds": 33.6,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's post-viral fatigue, and we'll know more once the a thyroid test is back. I think a thyroid test makes sense here, for fatigue. I'm sending you for blood tests because of fatigue. Pace yourself, a little more activity each day but stop before you're wiped out. Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.76,
      "end_seconds": 348.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in a month any last questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 349.78,
      "end_seconds": 351.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "Thanks so much, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.9,
      "end_seconds": 354.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "Bye for now."
    }
  ]
}